{
  "title": "Ingredient parser: the alternative's size word stays in the item after \"N large or M <size> <food>\"",
  "description": "Lines like \"2 large or 3 smaller leeks\", \"1 large or 2 thin carrots\", \"3 large or 4 regular cloves garlic\", \"5 large or 6 medium-sized lemons\" and \"4 large or 5 small-medium apples\" now parse the alternative count as a second measurement (amount, no unit), but the alternative's size word stays at the front of the item: \"smaller leeks\", \"thin carrots\", \"regular cloves garlic\", \"medium-sized lemons\", \"small-medium apples\". \
The catalog copes because catalog/resolve.rs LEADING_MODIFIERS now drops thin/slim/skinny/smaller/regular, but the shopping list shows the size word, and the alternative measurement loses its size (it should read like \"3 small\", not a bare \"3\"). \
Fix in ingredient_parser/mod.rs Step 4.5 (the \"or\" alternative): when the primary unit is a size (is_size_unit) and the alternative is a bare count followed by a size-like adjective, take that adjective as the alternative's unit. \
Expect intentional data/ diffs from make pipeline.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
